##:
math -- the Sushi half of the math module.

The module has two halves. The functions (`sqrt`, `pow`, `abs`, `min`, `max` and the
others) and the constants are compiled into the stdlib bitcode; the methods of this file
on the integer types ship as Sushi source. A method of a built-in type needs no import,
so `a.divmod(b)` works with no `use <math>`.
:##

##:
Divides the value by `b` and gives the quotient and the remainder, the same as `/` and `%`.

A `b` of 0 stops the program with a runtime error, the same as `/`.

- Parameter b: The divisor.
- Returns: The pair `(self / b, self % b)`.
- Example:
  ```sushi
  let i8 n = 7
  let (q, r) = n.divmod(2)
  println("{q} {r}")
  ```
:##
public extend i8 divmod(i8 b) (i8, i8):
    return (self / b, self % b)

